course: dictionary
lesson: 14504
title: Pelage: an animal's fur
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Pelage is a formal word from science. It means the fur, hair or wool that covers a mammal's body. A mammal is an animal that has fur or hair, such as a fox, a rabbit or a seal.
explain: Look for clues in the sentence. «The Arctic fox's pelage turns white in winter.» The sentence is about the fox's covering, so pelage must be its fur. Test it: «The Arctic fox's fur turns white in winter» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Pelage is a word you will meet in nature books and science lessons more than in everyday talk. «The hare's pelage is brown in summer, so it blends in with the grass.» The brown fur helps the hare hide.
fact: Pelage means the fur, hair or wool covering a mammal's body.
fact: «Pelage» is a formal word used by zoologists, the scientists who study animals.
fact: «The Arctic fox's pelage turns white in winter and brown in summer.»
fact: In lessons on adaptations, pelage helps animals keep warm and hide.
fact: Pelage is uncountable, so we say «the pelage», not «a pelage» or «two pelages».
exercise: «The Arctic fox's pelage turns white in winter.» What does pelage mean? | The sound a fox makes | *The fur covering the fox's body | The fox's tail | The fox's den under the snow
exercise: «The seal's thick pelage keeps it warm in icy water.» What job does the pelage do? | It holds the seal's food | It makes a loud noise | It helps the seal fly | *It keeps the seal warm
exercise: Ella says, «Pelage is a bird's nest.» Is she right? | Yes, because nests are made of soft things | Yes, it is the word for a home | *No, pelage is the fur, hair or wool covering a mammal's body | No, it is the word for a bird's song
test: «The rabbit's pelage is soft and thick in winter.» What does pelage mean? | *The fur covering the rabbit's body | The rabbit's burrow under the ground | The rabbit's long ears | The rabbit's favourite food
test: Why does a mammal's pelage help it in cold places? | It stops the mammal from needing food | It makes the mammal faster than the wind | *It keeps the mammal warm | It lets the mammal fly
exam: Which word means the fur covering a mammal's body? | beak | scales | shell | *pelage
